  "result": "I've written a plan for the `#` bug but haven't changed any code. Nothing has been run either, so the cause below comes from reading the code. Plan mode is on, and `ExitPlanMode` isn't available in this session, so I can't submit the plan for approval the usual way. Tell me to proceed and I'll make the edit.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py:603` builds its `shlex.shlex` object directly. That leaves `shlex`'s default comment character, `#`, switched on. Everything from the first `#` onward is silently dropped. Bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell completion all split the command line through this function, so all four are affected.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. Add `lex.commenters = \"\"` right after `lex = shlex.shlex(string, posix=True)` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`.\n2. Add two cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `\"cli a#b\"` should give `[\"cli\", \"a#b\"]`, and `\"cli #x\"` should give `[\"cli\", \"#x\"]`.\n3. Optionally add a changelog entry.\n\nI would check it by running `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py`, then the full suite. The new cases should fail before the fix and pass after it.\n\n**Out of scope:** The exploration also turned up two separate quoting problems that I'm leaving alone. The bash script's unquoted `COMPREPLY+=($value)` breaks on values with spaces or glob characters. The fish script splits on every comma, which truncates values that contain one.\n\nThe full plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-twinkling-wall.md`.",
